\f1\fs22 The food went cold under their warming domes, which Chanta felt was a contradiction the kitchen ought to have solved by now, and for a while he sat in the wreckage of the perfect evening and waited for the door to reconsider. It didn\'92t. Doors, he was learning, were the one thing in the building all the money in the world hadn\'92t taught any manners.\
