As far as he could tell, all of the Elvi in the locker were the same series, evenly divided by gender. The second locker contained Kid Galahad series Elvi, the third, It Happened at the World\'92s Fair. After finding nothing but Flaming Star boxes in the next, Chanta marched down the aisle, pushing his increasing sense of loss into his stomach, that things he loved were not things the world had ever intended to keep in stock. He scanned the lockers, hoping to see even the smallest sign any of them were different. At the end of the aisle he checked the map on his tablet, found his bearings, took the cross-aisle, then followed the route two aisles over.\
He stopped, reluctant to just walk out. He pulled out his tablet again. \'93Hey, stupid. Can you give me provisioning stock levels in the bunker?\'94\
His tablet answered nothing for a few long seconds, then: \'93
\f2\i Stupid
\f1\i0  is rich, from a man who counts on his fingers and still runs out. But sure. Provisioning Level, summarised. The full manifest runs nine hundred thousand pages, and you are not a nine-hundred-thousand-page reader: Food: roughly eleven thousand years of it, for one mouth\'85\'94\
\'93Stop!\'94\
\'93 \'859,412 sides of bacon...\'94\
\'93Shut up. Just answer me: how many Elvis units are there, Harum Scarum series.\'94\
\'93Sure, I\'92ll look that up for you.\'94\
Chanta waited as many seconds as his impatience could afford to spend. \'93Well?\'94\
After a few more seconds, the tablet answered, \'93Zero.\'94\
\'93What? Are you telling me there are stacks and rows of Elvis units in here, but zero Harum Scarums?\'94\
There was a pause. \'93I didn\'92t actually check the numbers, but extrapolated from the numbers of the three most popular Elvis series.\'94\
\'93Can\'92t you check the inventory?\'94\
\'93You should have been more specific in your request.\'94\
\'93Check the inventory.\'94\
\'93Checking. One moment.\'94 More than one moment passed before the tablet said, \'93Accessing Inventory and purchase order records ... the number of Harum Scarums that have ever been stored in the bunker is \'85 zero. Could I interest you in a more popular series?\'94\
Chanta rammed the tablet back in his pocket and resumed the exit route from memory. In the final aisle, he realised he was approaching the service lift block from behind.\
The last half of the aisle was stacked with the same stasis lockers the food and Elvi were being preserved in. He strode past most of them but, in the end, couldn\'92t resist checking one more locker before he gave up.\
Yep, there were Grayling Corp coffin-shaped boxes in there, just as Chanta suspected. Except these all had a large, cheerful, orange starburst-shaped sticker slapped on their sides, with a message shouting, 
\f4\i\b\fs20 NOW WITH NEW PINK TIE!
